# Internationalization (web)

## Rule

**No hardcoded user-facing strings** in `apps/web/` — labels, buttons, headings, errors, toasts, empty states, table headers, aria-labels, placeholders.

All copy lives in locale message files and is rendered via **next-intl**.

## Setup

| File | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `apps/web/i18n/request.ts` | `getRequestConfig` — loads `messages/en.json` (MVP locale `en`) |
| `apps/web/next.config.ts` | `createNextIntlPlugin('./i18n/request.ts')` |
| `apps/web/app/layout.tsx` | `NextIntlClientProvider` + `generateMetadata` via `getTranslations` |

No `[locale]` URL segment in MVP — single default locale `en`.

## Required pattern

```tsx
import { useTranslations } from "next-intl";

export function Example() {
  const t = useTranslations("repos");
  return <h1>{t("title")}</h1>;
}
```

Server components: `getTranslations` from `next-intl/server`.

## Message files

| Path | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `apps/web/messages/en.json` | English (MVP default locale) |
| `apps/web/messages/<locale>.json` | Additional locales when added |

### Namespaces (top-level keys in `en.json`)

`common`, `auth`, `dashboard`, `repos`, `integrations`, `ticket-projects`, `notifications`, `settings`

Key naming within a namespace: `feature.element` — e.g. `dashboard.runPoll`, `integrations.testConnection`.

## Allowed literals (not i18n violations)

- CSS class names, `data-testid`, route paths (`/repos`)
- Technical IDs from API (`sourceKind`, UUIDs)
- `aria-hidden` decorative symbols with no semantic meaning
- Log/debug strings in non-UI code

## Forbidden

- JSX text nodes with English copy: `<Button>Save</Button>`
- `title="Delete integration"` on components
- `toast("Settings saved")` — use `t("settings.saved")`
- Duplicating the same string in multiple files without a message key

## ESLint

`apps/web/eslint.config.mjs` extends `eslint-plugin-i18next` flat recommended config:

- Rule: `i18next/no-literal-string` — **error** on JSX text literals
- Message files (`messages/**`) are ignored by ESLint

`npm run lint` must pass before commit.

## Spec

See `docs/specs.html#i18n`.
